{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfd8f7jofo","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"bench DAG variant design — wire and judge per task then DAG only context","summary":"User approved creating a second bench variant (bench-economy-dag.js) alongside the existing bench-economy.js. The existing bench (RAG variant) stays as-is: ON arm uses cold search_knowledge during execution. The new DAG variant: ON arm runs suggest_links → add_dependency → get_dependency_summaries → injects those summaries into the agent's initial prompt. No live search_knowledge call during agent execution — context arrives pre-loaded exactly as the dispatcher does it in production. OFF arm identical to current. Same 11 scenarios, same N. Key hypothesis: DAG-injected overhead < 1.78× RAG overhead because (1) no extra tool call during execution, (2) more targeted context, (3) KB-neutral tasks get zero injection if suggest_links finds no relevant deps. The paper will compare both variants: RAG overhead vs DAG overhead vs OFF baseline.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T15:26:11.455Z","vec":[-0.15063342452049255,0.016250016167759895,-0.011025698855519295,0.05205875635147095,-0.009929806925356388,-0.0664355605840683,0.02017924375832081,0.07918643951416016,-0.016866274178028107,-0.011826644651591778,-0.034890543669462204,0.05165446549654007,-0.0386752188205719,-0.050344306975603104,0.04261131212115288,0.01868363842368126,0.1962047517299652,-0.04862092062830925,-0.02951318956911564,-0.0060293180868029594,0.0491802878677845,-0.025081174448132515,0.020559346303343773,-0.05987056344747543,0.04568544775247574,-0.06851399689912796,-0.08669048547744751,0.03258589282631874,0.07380858808755875,-0.0674082562327385,0.03268888592720032,0.06652652472257614,-0.05147852003574371,-0.00756198400631547,-0.06514477729797363,0.07931520789861679,0.004839739296585321,-0.01105297077447176,-0.017815709114074707,0.019647574052214622,0.07186044007539749,0.05546817556023598,0.00467984564602375,0.054636619985